<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Cenbank bond rate rises to 2.4697 pct.</title>
<headline>Brazil Cenbank bond rate rises to 2.4697 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's benchmark overnight rate rose to 2.4697 percent a month, from 2.4508 percent last week, at today's 6.31 billion reais sale of 56-day Central Bank Bonds (BBC), dealers said.</p>
<p>The 56-day bonds will mature on February 12. Today's auction is expected to add 1.190 billion reais to the banking system, with 7.5 billion reais in old bonds coming due Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5418</p>
